  The Gold Falcon Utilities:
  
   The GOLD FALCON UTILITIES is a set of irreplaceable helpers for 
   the Spectrum Holobyte family of flight simulators! Formerly 
   commercial, now shareware, it includes the latest versions of 
   FalcCalc, F3Maps, F3 Requisition, Show F3, and GFU Menu. This 
   fully integrated package brings out many of the best features of 
   Falcon 3.0, MiG-29, and Hornet.
   
   You can find this shareware file (usually called GFUTIL.ZIP) on 
   better BBS systems everywhere.

  Strategic Falcon and Strategic MiG:
 
   Tactical Features
    
    Fly any allied aircraft in Falcon 3.0! Version 1.21a of 
    StratFalc allows you to change the type of aircraft *you* 
    fly--you can pilot, for example, A-10s for CAS runs, F-4s for 
    SEAD, or B-52s for bombing! Although the cockpit will still 
    look like an F-16, all external views of the aircraft and, 
    especially, the aircraft's flight model will be that of the new 
    plane!
    
    Add, remove, or alter F-16 flights, much like in Falcon 3.0 
    itself, with some important additions: Fuel remaining and Time 
    to Waypoint are always displayed.
    
    Change the location of F-16 starting and ending waypoints 
    (these are normally "locked" in Falcon itself).
    
    Add, remove, or alter Allied or Enemy flights.
    
    Change the types of aircraft for any flight in this mission. 
    (Although your "personal plane" must always be an F-16.)
    
    Change the waypoints of any flight--F-16, allied, or enemy-- 
    involved in a mission.
    
    Change the temperament and skill levels of any allied or enemy 
    pilot.
    
    Change the weapon loadout of any aircraft involved.
    
    Add or remove ground paths and ground units.
    
    Change the types, waypoints, and temperament of any ground 
    units.
    
    Make ground columns more realistic; no more "kill me fast" 
    in-line formations.
    
    Limit the number of SA-7s you face.
    
    View the mission description with the press of a key.
    
    Check mission timing with the "synchronized timing trace" 
    feature, which shows with graphical/animated symbols where each 
    flight in the mission will be in relation to each other!
    
    Swap your F-16 flight waypoints with those of any other F-16 
    flight--useful when you don't want to fly the lead mission.
    
    Load every plane correctly and automatically--up to 18 preset 
    loadouts for each plane type!
    
   Strategic Features
    
    Change the occupation of any site, to instantly capture nodes 
    or surrender them to the enemy.
    
    Change the current strength or capacity of any site.
    
    Change the rate of growth of any site.
    
    Change the quantity of specific unit types at a site (the 
    site's "breakdown").
    
    Change the node structure for the theater. You can cut any site 
    off from resupply.
    
    Change which nodes mean victory and which spell defeat.
    
    You can even fully randomize victory/defeat sites!
    
    Launch an automatic, coordinated ground attack against any site.
    
    Simulation Mode changes the way you play Falcon! Aircraft 
    squadrons are assigned to bases--you can transfer at will-- but 
    your resources are limited! Three brigades await your orders, 
    but if you screw up, they pay!
    
   Other Features
    
    Change the current weather and the altitude of the cloud cover. 
    Also change the predicted weather.
    
    Change the home air base--you can fly a campaign from any 
    allied-occupied strip.
    
    Place an ILS at any base.
    
    Change the current day and time.
    
    Change the resupply and replacement days and times.
    
    Change the campaign momentum, both macro and micro--turn the 
    tide on the enemy.
    
    Learn to properly use the "Kill Boxes" which have always been 
    present in Falcon 3.0.
    
    If you wish, all enemy-related information can be hidden from 
    you by checking a single box.
    
    Run Falcon or any series of programs with the press of a key 
    and automatically return to StratFalc when you're done.
    
   System Requirements: 
    
    The program is entirely graphical; to use it you *must* have a 
    mouse. It also requires Falcon 3.0, any version from 3.01.1 
    through 3.05.

  Strategic MiG:                                     
    
    Take all the above information about StratFalc, view it from 
    the other side, add new missiles (anti-runway, anti-radiation), 
    and you've got StratMiG. It supports MiG 1.03 and 1.04.

